    "historicalContext": "Cadillac used its second home weekend at COTA to evaluate small floor and cooling updates, but the bumpy circuit kept the MAC-26's setup and tyre window narrow. After Colton Herta's FP1 programme and a broad setup search, both race drivers extracted the available package in qualifying, yet the one-lap gap to Williams remained: Pérez lost roughly two tenths in the final sector when a KERS issue coincided with traffic at the final corner, while Bottas said the team had at least found a workable balance. They qualified P21 and P22 before the final grid placed Pérez P18 and Bottas P19.",
